 ## 11\. LangGraph Workflow

 The LangGraph workflow contains three primary nodes:

 ### Retrieve

 Queries Pinecone using the user question and retrieves the most relevant document chunks.

 ### Generate

 Builds a prompt containing only the retrieved context and asks the LLM to answer using that context.

 ### Validate

 Checks whether the generated answer is supported by the retrieved context and combines the grounding result with retrieval relevance to produce a confidence indicator.

 Workflow:

```
START
  |
  v
Retrieve
  |
  v
Generate
  |
  v
Validate
  |
  v
END
```

 ## 12\. Grounding Strategy

 The chatbot is explicitly instructed not to use general knowledge when answering questions.

 If the retrieved context is insufficient, the chatbot responds:

```
I cannot answer based on the provided document.
```

 This behavior is important for preventing the application from functioning as an unrestricted general-purpose chatbot.

